":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/7F5CAXQA","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/YJCI8GY2?page=1&annotation=TV5VUVF3","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/YJCI8GY2?page=1&annotation=L6ZBFPXB","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/YJCI8GY2?page=1&annotation=ZCFPVVFD","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 10","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/YJCI8GY2?page=10&annotation=LKCR9K4W","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Challenges of diet planning for children using artificial intelligence","Authors":"Changhun Lee, Soohyeok Kim, Jayun Kim, Chiehyeon Lim, Minyoung Jung","Year":2022,"DOI":"10.4162/nrp.2022.16.6.801","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"We developed 2 AI solutions for children aged 3–5 yrs using a generative adversarial network (GAN) model and a reinforcement learning (RL) framework.  After training these solutions to produce daily diet plans, experts evaluated the human- and AI-generated diets in 2 steps.","Findings":"In the evaluation of adequacy of nutrition, where experts were provided only with nutrient information and no food names, the proportion of strong positive responses to RLgenerated diets was higher than that of the human- and GAN-generated diets (P < 0.001). In contrast, in terms of diet composition, the experts’ responses to human-designed diets were more positive when experts were provided with food name information (i.e., composition information).","Conclusions":"This study demonstrates the possibility of developing AI-assisted diet planning methods for children and highlights the importance of composition compliance in diet planning. Further integrative cooperation in the fields of nutrition, engineering, and medicine is needed to improve the suitability of our proposed AI solutions and benefit children’s well-being by providing high-quality diet planning in terms of both compositional and nutritional criteriaWe found that the developed AI was superior to human nutritionists in designing nutritionally appropriate diet plans, but inferior in terms of compositional quality. Further integrative expert cooperation among dieticians, engineers, and pediatricians is needed to improve the capability of the proposed AI solution in order to satisfy expectations relating to meal composition and to benefit the well-being of children.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1mknzro","at":1774939548501}},"smart_blocks:Augmented Dietitian Okunmuşlar/leeChallengesDietPlanning2022a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.06926215,-0.0245749,0.00394083,0.00634152,-0.02818476,0.03155451,-0.03178646,0.02125342,-0.0015329,-0.01986962,-0.00408641,-0.07926269,0.05578556,0.0499084,0.09630171,0.0032702,-0.00879743,0.01951214,-0.02919779,-0.01723261,0.05272746,-0.05034044,0.00507512,-0.03299316,0.02547937,0.05143339,-0.035162,-0.06834961,-0.02141996,-0.22506787,0.05446941,-0.0130074,0.07008734,-0.02833024,-0.0615455,0.07278163,-0.02954288,0.04922463,-0.02493267,0.0244836,0.00925173,0.02959344,0.00462244,-0.00078378,0.00635583,-0.00263837,-0.05042648,-0.02217012,-0.07627357,-0.04520999,-0.0161458,-0.0502142,0.01562003,0.05398039,0.042006,0.04597482,0.0299621,0.03337556,0.05616873,0.08500436,0.01685243,0.06913091,-0.19014829,0.1006496,-0.00723435,0.06390449,-0.06380194,0.01742638,0.01568926,-0.01444988,-0.03791203,0.00984975,0.06182698,0.02735945,-0.01630204,0.04164825,0.04721322,-0.0727392,0.02926175,-0.02848149,0.00007512,0.05761392,-0.06285318,0.02327945,-0.03719528,0.02291854,-0.03525307,-0.08316527,0.06835701,-0.00652606,-0.01527509,-0.0068143,-0.01073504,0.01388131,0.0238621,-0.01137848,-0.03957633,-0.04600569,-0.10010704,0.11682698,-0.01825343,-0.00626116,0.0271162,0.01142548,0.00329247,-0.07498763,-0.0